                <pb facs="0094" n="22" xml:id="pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14867/8.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Rives to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-09-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 30,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Rives says he has been requested by the minister for foreign affairs to ask
                    that the United States customs authorities accept certificates of chambers of
                    commerce of Austria-Hungary and extend to Austria-Hungary the same privileges,
                    as to Germany, until enforcement of Payne bill, and requests answer by
                    cable.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
